# Copy to .env.local (which git ignores) when you want the extension's donation panel
# to talk to a locally running payment site instead of production.
#
#   cd ../../Intelligent-Workspace-Web && pnpm run cert   # once, self-signed
#   cd ../../Intelligent-Workspace-Web && pnpm dev
#
# HTTPS, not HTTP. Chrome refuses to autofill a payment form that is not in a secure
# context, and the panel framing an http:// origin makes the whole chain insecure — the
# card fields then say "autofill is disabled because this form does not use a secure
# connection". `pnpm run cert` in the site's repository writes the certificate that
# `astro dev` picks up. The certificate is self-signed, so open https://localhost:4321
# once in a tab and accept the warning before the panel can frame it.
#
# Then rebuild the extension. Leave this unset for any build you intend to publish:
# production is the default precisely so that nobody has to remember to switch it back.
VITE_PAYMENT_ORIGIN=https://localhost:4321
